  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-09-20T16:24:04.843Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "At the moment the default for physbones is set up for good ponytail (and maybe some tails?) physics. However, avatar developers use physbones for a lot and end up having to learn precise tuning numbers (or rely on community knowledge and screenshots of settings) to get acceptable results. This is labourious and really not fun.\n\nFor normal VRChat stuff there's really only a few types of physbone use:\n\n* Ponytails/long hair\n\n* Bangs/front hair\n\n* Hanging clothing like ties or skirts\n\n* Tails\n\n* Chest movement\n\n* Satchels and other heavier stuff\n\nIt'd be nice just to have some presets in the script that creators can lean on as starting points. \n\nLikewise the default we currently have has a zero set for its value that dampens all/world movement. This simply doesn't work for most uses of physbones in client and is a common reason why you see otherwise normal avatars look terrible when locomoting around a world. Defaults really should use this damping!\n\nIt would also be good for the physbones script to link to a documentation page that can help users actually get good results. Ideally, this would cover common stuff like cloth and hair.",
